  "plan": "Wait for/retrieve the full help output. Then examine it carefully for the mode listing. I will scroll/grep to ensure I see the complete listing rather than a truncated view.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "rencrypt --help 2>&1 | cat\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The usage is `rencrypt [-o OUTPUT] [-p PROTOCOL] [-v] input_files`. The protocol/mode is selected via `-p PROTOCOL`, but --help doesn't list available protocols or their security properties. I must not guess. I need to discover the protocol list and documented security properties from the tool itself or its source.",
  "plan": "Investigate how to list protocols: try `rencrypt -p help`, `rencrypt --list`, and inspect the rencrypt binary/source for a list of protocols with their security descriptions. Since it's at /usr/local/bin, check if it's a script and read it.",
